  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <h3>Is SOC Analyst suitable for beginners?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Beginners can start by learning networking, operating systems and cybersecurity fundamentals before moving to security monitoring and incident investigation.</p>

  <h3>Do I need to learn Linux for SOC jobs?</h3>
  <p>Linux knowledge is useful because security professionals may work with Linux systems, command-line tools and system logs.</p>

  <h3>Is coding compulsory for a SOC Analyst?</h3>
  <p>Not every entry-level role requires advanced coding. Basic scripting can be useful for automation and log analysis.</p>

  <h3>What should I learn first for a SOC Analyst career?</h3>
  <p>Start with networking, Windows and Linux fundamentals, then learn security concepts, log analysis and SIEM workflows.</p>

  <h2>Conclusion</h2>
  <p>A SOC Analyst career path combines networking, operating system knowledge, security monitoring and investigation skills. Build a strong foundation, practise in authorized labs and keep improving your technical knowledge.</p>

